ose and your  airway the systemic vaccine gets more of  your immune system engaged and  apparently does a better job of  preparing you if you're going to see  that virus again you said that data  settled issue data from all over  including overseas the wall street  journal cites the uk data could be a  positive indication saying the latest  surge of covet 19 cases in uk is giving  rise to growing optimism among doctors  and scientists that the highly  transmissible delta variant of the  coronavirus can be held at bay with high  levels of vaccination and public caution  although case loads are now ticking  higher hospital admissions have been  falling deaths are a fraction of the  level seen in earlier phases of the  pandemic in other words the u.k other  places had seen a major spike but that  is really falling off  as time goes on is that what we are to  look forward to  well one would hope i think it's really  hard to extrapolate from other countries  experience and you know i'm a little  concerned when i saw the uk spike come  down fairly quickly i was encouraged but  look at the last week or so it stopped  going down and it looks like it might be  going back up again this virus has so  many tricks that we haven't completely  figured out you know the bottom line  brett is if we in the united states want  to avoid more cases more  hospitalizations more deaths if there  was ever a wake-up call for the people  who have not gotten vaccinated yet this  is the moment find out how to get that  vaccine there's a place near you that  has it ready it's free it's available  there's no time to waste and we put that  up every day uh dr collins last thing  you know as more and more information  comes out um i remember your skepticism  the emails you sent dr fauci at the  beginning and we've gone over that we've  asked you that about  the covet origins and  the skepticism about it coming from the  lab and you clarified that you thought  it was  not a weaponized thing from the c